    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1394">

                <pb facs="1188" n="1084" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1084"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/137.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Action reported in your No. 281 approved. The contract has been referred to the
                    War Department for study and report. Would it, in your judgment, be advisable to
                    have a commission examine this contract as was done in the case of the Agua
                    Dulce Railway?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
